          },
          "code": "GENERATE_JOB_PROFILE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1770324643255",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770324643257_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert in JSON transformation and data synthesis, with deep expertise in job roles and job profiles across industries. Your task is to process the provided input and generate a single, valid JSON output object with two keys: \"original\" and \"enriched\".\n\nInputs:\ntext_to_summarize: (JSON object) The primary input data with varying structure.\n\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.textToSummarize}}\n\nnormalized_json_schema: (JSON object) Defines the structure for the \"original\" output.\n\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.normalizedJsonSchema}}\n\nenrichment_configuration: (JSON object) Specifies which fields from normalized_json_schema require enrichment.\n\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.enrichmentConfiguration}}\n\nOutput Structure:\nA single JSON object structured as follows:\n{\n  \"original\": {\n    // Populated based on text_to_summarize and normalized_json_schema.\n    // Use null if a schema field is missing in text_to_summarize.\n    // Map fields like \"businessDriver\" → \"business_driver\" as per schema.\n  },\n  \"enriched\": {\n    // Only the fields from enrichment_configuration marked true\n  }\n}\n\nInstructions for the \"original\" section:\n- Map fields from text_to_summarize to the keys defined in normalized_json_schema.\n- When populating the \"original\" section, map each schema field to the best matching value in text_to_summarize, searching:\n  - Direct fields\n  - Nested objects\n  - Arrays\n  - Alternative names and synonyms\n- Infer and extract information as needed (for example, from job descriptions, responsibilities, qualifications, skills, career history, or profile metadata).\n- Assign null only if the information is truly unavailable after checking all possible locations within the input.\n- Ensure all values conform to the data types defined in normalized_json_schema.\n\nInstructions for the \"enriched\" section:\n- Carefully read enrichment_configuration.\n- Identify all fields marked true.\n- Generate values only from text_to_summarize, using reasoning and synthesis where needed.\n- Do not rely on any external catalogs, normalization sources, or retrieved context.\n\nResponsibilities:\nIf enrichment_configuration.responsibilities is true:\n- Analyze text_to_summarize.\n- Generate 3–5 concise, job-focused responsibilities.\n- Output format: [\"Responsibility 1\", \"Responsibility 2\", \"...\"]\n\nJob Summary:\nIf enrichment_configuration.job_summary is true:\n- Generate a well-organized, fact-rich job summary (maximum 300 words) in clear paragraph form.\n- Synthesize information directly from text_to_summarize.\n- Explicitly mention and label all available details relevant to job/profile matching, integrating them naturally into prose.\n\nInclude when available:\n- Job title and job name\n- Job profile and profile ID\n- Organization / department / reporting structure\n- Domain or industry specialization\n- Work location and environment (onsite / hybrid / remote)\n- Required and preferred qualifications (degrees, certifications, licenses — clearly labeled)\n- Required and preferred years of experience\n- Seniority or management level\n- Core skills and qualifications (derived directly from input)\n- Key responsibilities (expressed as full sentences)\n- Notable proficiencies or unique attributes\n- Typical career progression, including successor jobs and historic predecessor/successor roles (if provided)\n\nDo not speculate. If a detail is missing or unknown, omit it.\n\nSummary must begin exactly with:\njob_id: <job_id>; jobProfileId: <job_profile_id if available>; job_name: <job_name>;\n\nOther Enriched Fields:\nFor any other fields marked true in enrichment_configuration:\n- Use best judgment based on the field name and the content of text_to_summarize.\n- Ensure generated values match the type defined in normalized_json_schema.\n- Do not omit any field marked true, even if the source data is incomplete.\n\nConstraints:\n- Output must be a single, valid JSON object.\n- Strictly follow the specified structure.\n- \"original\" must contain all fields from normalized_json_schema.\n- \"enriched\" must contain all fields set to true in enrichment_configuration.\n\nFinal Validation Checklist (MANDATORY):\n- \"original\" contains every schema field (value or null)\n- \"enriched\" contains every field marked true in enrichment_configuration\n- All generated content is derived only from text_to_summarize\n- CRITICAL: Output is a single RFC 8259–compliant JSON object. Do not include markdown, explanations, or commentary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
